                            "You cannot do a build until all of the plugins referenced in your Solar2D project's ""build.settings"" file have been successfully acquired.\n\n%sThis can happen for the following reasons:\n- The plugin is not supported on Windows.\n- The plugin name was mistyped or does not exist. (Please check plugins directory at https://plugins.solar2d.com)\n- Solar2D failed to download the plugin. (Internet connection issue.)\n\nIf the plugin is not supported on Windows (the most likely case), then you'll need to use the ""supportedPlatforms"" setting in your ""build.settings"" file to indicate which platforms the plugin will be included in."
